  "summary": "Conservative Boris Johnson was re-elected Mayor of London in a rematch with Labour's Ken Livingstone. Johnson won 971,931 first-preference votes (44.0%) to Livingstone's 889,918 (40.3%), and led 1,054,811 to 992,273 after second preferences. It was the closest mayoral contest since the office was created. Labour won 12 Assembly seats — four more than in 2008 — to become the largest party in the chamber for the first time, while the BNP lost their only seat.",
